			"Message": "refactor(Element): Sync submodules with PascalCase naming convention\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with PascalCase refactoring:\n- Air: Rename CLI handlers (handle_status → Status, handle_restart → Restart, handle_config → Config, handle_metrics → Metrics, handle_logs → Logs, handle_debug → Debug) and plugin trait methods (handle_message → Message, handle_event → Event)\n- Grove: Rename handle_call → Call in APIBridgeImpl\n- Mountain: Rename IPC handler functions (handle_commands_execute → CommandsExecute, handle_configuration_get → ConfigurationGet, handle_incoming_message → IncomingMessage, etc.)\n- Sky: Add event-driven installation path for Wind's LandWorkbench bridge that listens for cel:services-ready, ensuring proper sequencing: services DI container populated → install Wind bridge → notify subscribers\n\nThese changes align with the project's naming convention specified in CLAUDE.md, removing handle_ prefixes for shorter, consistent method names across the codebase.",
			"SHA": "1d6badc56b52760aa91f3c847a1ae95c869aeb4a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:18:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				109,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Element): Batch command registration to eliminate IPC saturation during extension boot\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with coordinated performance fixes addressing keystroke lag during extension boot:\n- Mountain: Add CommandEmitBatch to buffer 1000+ registerCommand notifications and flush after 16ms, reducing individual emit storms to a single batched IPC round-trip\n- Output: Revert DisableLazyPaint opt-in gate (regressed editor mount) and remove PartZIndexCSS `isolation: isolate` rule that blocked input events under WKWebView\n- Sky: Accept batched `{ commands: [...] }` format alongside legacy single-command shape via new RegisterOneCommand helper\n- Cocoon: Sync to latest\n\nThese changes prevent 1000+ Tauri events per extension boot from saturating the shared WKWebView IPC channel that also delivers keystrokes, restoring input responsiveness during the most resource-intensive phase.\n\nRefs: Related to #10785a0 (IPC channel saturation), #9cae17e (lazy paint RAF/IO overrides)",
			"SHA": "ee7ae2629ee433d18040d6fd237bf9d2e1c28c70"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T00:36:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				109,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Make DisableLazyPaint RAF/IO overrides opt-in\n\nWrap the requestAnimationFrame and IntersectionObserver overrides in a conditional guard, requiring `__LAND_AGGRESSIVE_LAZY_PAINT__ = true` to be set BEFORE workbench bootstrap. These overrides redirect Monaco's rAF callbacks to the macrotask queue and replace native IntersectionObserver with a fire-on-observe stub that calls getBoundingClientRect() synchronously. The problem: both bypass WKWebView's compositor-frame coordination—which also delivers keyboard input. Once Monaco starts rendering (theme load, decorations, cursor blink, minimap, scrollbars), the macrotask queue floods and keystrokes starve, causing the input lag symptom this polyfill was meant to solve. Keep the CSS lazy-paint kill (content-visibility: visible) always applied—it solves the original \"panels invisible until hover/scroll\" WKWebView bug without affecting input latency. This complements the recent IPC logging fix (2588fe4) and EditContext polyfill (44e160c) in addressing WKWebView input starvation.",
			"SHA": "9cae17ed70c86ca51f9b79df42ce6ccf4e14a1b7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T00:16:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				109,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Element): Reduce IPC channel saturation to fix keystroke lag during extension boot\n\nSynchronize five Element submodules with performance optimizations addressing input lag caused by IPC channel saturation:\n- Mountain: Gate mountain_sync_status_update and mountain_performance_update events behind LAND_SYNC_STATUS_EMIT and LAND_PERF_EMIT env vars. Add subscriber fast-path to skip lock-and-drain when Subscribers.is_empty().\n- Output: Remove success-case tauri-invoke logging in InvokeMountain and fire-and-forget channel stub logging. Only log drift disposition.\n- Sky: Remove per-fire _CelDispatchLog traces (now requires __LAND_TRACE_CEL_DISPATCH__=true). Diagnostic bridges for markers-bridge and webview-bridge now only log on pushable=false or hasRegister=false.\n- Wind: Remove success-case tauri-invoke forward (failures still forwarded). Only forward drift disposition case.\n\nThese changes prevent 50-100 log/emits per second during extension boot from saturating Tauri's invoke channel and starving keystroke delivery on the shared WebKit message channel.",
			"SHA": "10785a06a6996e30792a4a1818f5be6db75fd5c3"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780336593246
}